{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games","id":1482448,"title":"How often do players create shovelheads in your games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-30T20:30:15-07:00","id":1482448,"title":"How often do players create shovelheads in your games?","content":"My players created several last game, which lead to a fun scene in which they gave those shovelheads the drill sergeant from hell treatment ala &quot;Full Metal Jacket&quot;. How often are shovelheads part of your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T21:06:19-07:00","id":1482455,"title":"","content":"There was one game where the coterie used a &quot;honey pot&quot; character to ghoul and dominate a military base commander. Told the commander to set up a series of security drills and to make the base go dark for a weekend as part of it. The entire base staff was told to show up for medical exams friday evening, the entire base combat population was turned that night. Saturday night was spent teaching them to function and eating the remaining mortals. Sunday night they destroyed every identified Camarilla position within 4 hours flight/drive time of the base.<br /> <br /> The base commander sent out notifications to the relevant families that there were casualties during a training exercise and then apparently committed suicide before an investigation could be launched. The surviving shovel heads got absorbed into the sabbat as normal. The government didn't know what to do so they covered up the fact that an entire base worth of soldiers and equipment vanished over a weekend.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the ST didn't quite know how to handle that sort of approach to mass embracing. Shovel heads as idiotic gang members or homeless people who are mass embraced is fine if you want to play a &quot;Lost Boys&quot; grade street level game, not so much if you want to actually get something done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T23:01:43-07:00","id":1482464,"title":"","content":"My answer would be &quot;always&quot;. However, I can't honestly answer your question because 1) I don't run or play in Sabbat games, and 2) when I ST (Camarilla games where the Sabbat are just NPCs) I prefer the original portrayal of the Sabbat rather than late 2e/Revised. Originally all (or almost all) Sabbat were put through the Creation Rites. The Revised era was responsible for saying that was not really the case and only used in times of war, and I felt it transformed the Sabbat into the Camarilla-lite.<br /> <br /> That built on something that began in late 2e when the clanbooks for the Lasombra and Tzimisce came out. By that time, Andrew Greenberg was no longer Developer, and I feel the new powers that be didn't really believe in the unique elements of the Sabbat. For some odd reason, those clanbooks presented these Sabbat clans as acting very similar to the Camarilla clans. We got very little of the unique culture of the Sabbat in them. Their version of the Lasombra and Tzimisce was basically the same as if they were Camarilla clans with little distinction between the Sabbat version and their antri-tribu. Prior to those first clanbooks, there was a very heavy emphasis on the random nature of Sabbat embraces.<br /> <br /> The first Sabbat we ever meet In Chicago By Night are random embraces. Phillipe Rigaud was just an random soldier in camp when Sabbat arrived and picked him after reading his unconscious mind. Although selected to a degree, it was just because he best fit their criteria for cannon fodder in some random army camp. Wendy Wade just had the misfortune of staying out too late at the local singles bar. When 2e CbN came out and we met a Nomad Pack, we see mostly other random embraces. Cameron was just grabbed off the streets and despite being a &quot;loser&quot; was embraced by a Lasombra. The other members aren't even given descriptions to their embrace although it's likely just as random. The only member who was actually selected for embrace by his sire... was the mortal servant of a Sabbat Infernalist and therefore picked to deliberately carry out the demon's goals.<br /> <br /> Now the original Sabbat Players Guide is a bit of a mixed bag. While conforming to the rule of random embraces in time of war, they do say that in times of peace the True Sabbat do choose &quot;more carefully&quot;. But this is supposed to be done by two members of the Pack and &quot;carefully&quot; means they observe them for a few days or weeks. So not very carefully in my opinion. It is less random, but not too much. They just aren't spending the time needed to evaluate a particular mortal to decide if they are &quot;worthy&quot;, and not all pack members make picks. It's still fairly superficial criteria.<br /> <br /> I think this works fine for the Sabbat. They have a great turnover (including even whether the person they picked will even survive the Creation Rites) so it doesn't pay to be selective. If you spent a long time agonizing over who to embrace, you'll be disappointed after your Lupine hunt destroyed most of the pack. Or if they mouth off and is slain in Monomacy. Or any other of the many stupid ass violence the Sabbat perpetrate and gets so many members killed quickly.<br /> <br /> I also liked it because if was the closest thing we had to traditional vampire movies when anyone the vampire fed on became a vampire. You didn't need to be &quot;special&quot; to become a vampire. You just had to have bad luck by being in the wrong place at the wrong time.<br /> <br /> That also fit an important theme to the Sabbat which is that humanity is unimportant. Only being a vampire is important. What one was like as mortal had dubious value as to how well they'd succeed at being a vampire. The housewife might become a better Lasombra than the MBA graduate. Whereas there was often continuity between a character's mortal life and their undead existence for a Camarilla vampire, there was just a complete break for the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I liked that. It really defined the differences between the two sects.<br /> <br /> But the clanbooks and Revised just throw that out into the garbage bin by explaining that essentially the two sects acted the same except for perhaps the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> I think that was a huge mistake. It's important for the vampires in the two sects to act very differently, and different approaches to selecting new vampires was important to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T05:10:28-07:00","id":1482481,"title":"","content":"My general problem with shovelheads is that I don't buy this method being so effective in making for Vampires that embrace the sect's ideology to any degree, or see reason to devolve into violence so thoroughly so quickly. To me it would make sense that a considerable number of shovelheads aren't as easy to indoctrinate as a Pack expects and I never personally saw the books address that.<br /> <br /> Does it make sense that many, <i>maybe</i> most work? In a fictional setting, yes. I know it has a lot of brainwashing techniques there. It is a quick succession of shocking experiences, a lot of shouting and ritual, and there's the <i>Vinculum</i> as soon as possible. But I also know that brainwashing isn't all that effective all the time, specially fast techniques based on shock treatment and not customized for the target. The result may be the person accepting some of the stuff they're told at first and engaging on some activities, but hardly with any conviction and it wears down almost as fast.<br /> <br /> That's a briefing of my personal problem with the Creation Ritae as presented. I would personally prefer that it doesn't only have failure in the form of people not surviving it, but also a number of shovelheads that rebel almost immediately or soon after, and others that defect the Sect entirely during their first nights, and then explore how the Sabbat deal with them (and their freedom from their sires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:21:10-07:00","id":1482513,"title":"","content":"The way I run it is, the indoctrination isn't necessarily all that effective at first. However, it really doesn't need to be. The Vinculum makes them feel loyalty, their beast makes them feel an urge to kill, the Presence and high social traits of the Pack Priest do the rest adequately for the shovelhead's main purpose: charge that building and kill the Cammy/Anarch/werewolf inside it. <br /> <br /> The few who survive being used as canon-fodder can be slowly indoctrinated and watched carefully during the process.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, many will be spiraling down to wighthood, so training them in a path isn't just sect indoctrination, it's genuinely saving them from what amounts to a fatal cancer at that point.<br /> <br /> Even without the vinculum, and a Pack Priest with high Presence, they are going to be strongly inclined to want a cure to their impending wassail. Add the Vinculum and Presence on top of that, and it's not hard for me to believe at all that they would embrace Path of Enlightenment training with gusto.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T15:27:33-07:00","id":1482545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482513#post1482513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I run it is, the indoctrination isn't necessarily all that effective at first. However, it really doesn't need to be. The Vinculum makes them feel loyalty, their beast makes them feel an urge to kill, the Presence and high social traits of the Pack Priest do the rest adequately for the shovelhead's main purpose: charge that building and kill the Cammy/Anarch/werewolf inside it.<br /> <br /> The few who survive being used as canon-fodder can be slowly indoctrinated and watched carefully during the process.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, many will be spiraling down to wighthood, so training them in a path isn't just sect indoctrination, it's genuinely saving them from what amounts to a fatal cancer at that point.<br /> <br /> Even without the vinculum, and a Pack Priest with high Presence, they are going to be strongly inclined to want a cure to their impending wassail. Add the Vinculum and Presence on top of that, and it's not hard for me to believe at all that they would embrace Path of Enlightenment training with gusto.</div> </div> </div> </div>Averages are simplifications for groups that have Variance. Chances in bulk become Frequencies. Embracing people at random doesn't mean just that most of those won't seem like adequate candidates, it also means they're nobodies from <i>your</i> perspective, but in actuality are peoples of all stripes, with all sorts of baggage, morals and ways of dealing with new situations. If 90% of the population will respond as you predict under such circumstances if they survive and only 10% will become a problem, then every single Mass Embrace with at least 6 shovelheads in the end is more likely than not to produce a problem, and I'm being extremely generous with the numbers, even considering all the things you stated, and adding that I don't think every Pack has a Priest with Presence (this is the price you pay for anarchy, not every cell will follow the book as obvious at it seems).<br /> <br /> \u200bTake <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a>'s example for instance. In my head it is ludicrous to even think it had a chance to work. Getting an entire military base is staking your chances against you, royally. They've had military drilling doing the brainwash thing for far longer and more consistently, they are prepared to deal with all sorts of attacks, they've been prepared to the possibility of death and they have very clear duties to follow. All the effectiveness aside, you only need one of them rebelling at the right moment to bring down the whole operation in any of many ways, and a high probability of having more rebels than not.<br /> <br /> Paths after that have the same problem. One thing is for you to explain and paint a gruesome picture of what Wighthood is and what a Path can do to help. Another is the other person buying it. They have to believe you're honest, then they have to believe you're right, then they have to believe you have all the relevant information, then they have to lose all hope of unknown possibilities still existing, and then they have to really be able to muster the will to still go ahead, because they may have all sorts of reasons to really not want to from an emotional and even moral perspective, regardless of rational belief in this abstract threat (it isn't imaginary, but it is abstract). I don't see so many people buying into it, much less almost everyone in this position, specially if you consider how much dedication a Path demands.<br /> <br /> It isn't an attack on the notion or on Thoth's plot. I think it was well thought and fun as far as a game goes. It is just that <u><b>I</b></u><b><u> personally</u></b> do not buy it. Everyone has some things they find harder to suspend their disbelief, this is one such a thing for me. It doesn't mean I won't have Mass Embraces either, it is just that in my games it is far more complex to deal with the shovelheads, and every Pack has its own ways to deal with the actual results. The notion that shovelheads work almost seamlessly is another legend spread among the Camarilla. And the only reason my players never created shovelheads themselves is that <u>my players</u> never wanted to play as Sabbat. They're big fussed grognards that still see Requiem as a new fad that will go out soon and V20 (core) is just messing with a game that was pretty fine already... heck, we still stick to D&amp;D 3.5 for the gods' sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T16:57:15-07:00","id":1482552,"title":"","content":"If I'm running Sabbat with new guys. I always do it. Fun trick another gm tought me was to pick the players clan from what they do in early sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T17:45:54-07:00","id":1482556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482552#post1482552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm running Sabbat with new guys. I always do it. Fun trick another gm tought me was to pick the players clan from what they do in early sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't meant it as <i>your character is a shovelhead</i>, it was more <i>your character <b>embraces</b> shovelheads</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T18:07:32-07:00","id":1482558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482455#post1482455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was one game where the coterie used a &quot;honey pot&quot; character to ghoul and dominate a military base commander. Told the commander to set up a series of security drills and to make the base go dark for a weekend as part of it. The entire base staff was told to show up for medical exams friday evening, the entire base combat population was turned that night. Saturday night was spent teaching them to function and eating the remaining mortals. Sunday night they destroyed every identified Camarilla position within 4 hours flight/drive time of the base.<br /> <br /> The base commander sent out notifications to the relevant families that there were casualties during a training exercise and then apparently committed suicide before an investigation could be launched. The surviving shovel heads got absorbed into the sabbat as normal. The government didn't know what to do so they covered up the fact that an entire base worth of soldiers and equipment vanished over a weekend.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the ST didn't quite know how to handle that sort of approach to mass embracing. Shovel heads as idiotic gang members or homeless people who are mass embraced is fine if you want to play a &quot;Lost Boys&quot; grade street level game, not so much if you want to actually get something done.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's wildly more ambitious than what my players do. They found a family changing a busted tire on their way to Disney World, shovelheaded the five of them, and thought they were hot stuff for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T21:16:38-07:00","id":1482573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482481#post1482481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it make sense that many, <i>maybe</i> most work? In a fictional setting, yes. I know it has a lot of brainwashing techniques there. It is a quick succession of shocking experiences, a lot of shouting and ritual, and there's the <i>Vinculum</i> as soon as possible. But I also know that brainwashing isn't all that effective all the time, specially fast techniques based on shock treatment and not customized for the target. The result may be the person accepting some of the stuff they're told at first and engaging on some activities, but hardly with any conviction and it wears down almost as fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. This is why those who have been put through the Creation Rites are False Sabbat for an unspecified period of time before they become True Sabbat.<br /> <br /> There has to be a large amount of failures. Not every vampire is going to survive the Creation Rites. A fair number of those who do survive will fall to the Wassail, or be destroyed by the pack if they don't seem to be advancing quickly enough on their first few dots of a Path. And given the Sabbat is usually conspicuous in their violence, many are going to attract the attention of those who will destroy them - hunters, Camarilla archon groups like the Wolfpack, Lupines, and any other number of enemies.<br /> <br /> I don't believe that those who survive the Creation Rites are going to be loyal to the Sabbat &quot;just because&quot;. They'll be confused and disoriented and rely on their new &quot;friends&quot; for a while, but that isn't loyalty. The only way Sabbat brainwashing can work is in the long term, keeping them isolated and under watch. It'll likely be many weeks, months, or even years before their loyalty is assured. And in the meantime, a lot just aren't going to make it - they'll be destroyed at the hands of the Sabbat's enemies or by the Sabbat themselves because they obviously aren't working out. But I think the vinculum, the support they receive to help them withstand the Beast, love bombing and other cult indoctrination techniques, and the development of cool powers will help them adjust. They'll become loyal at least to their packmates, even if not to the Sabbat as a whole. (This is probably one reason the Sabbat is so fractious, and the sect always imploded.)<br /> <br /> The Sabbat isn't going to be able to rely on shovelheads to go after their enemies unless 1) they are able to make use of certain Disciplines to compel them, and 2) keep them hungry until the time they unleash them against their enemies because the Hunger alone will cause them to attack. This won't be easy and can easily backfire.<br /> <br /> The huge turnover of Sabbat neonates is one reason I have no interest to play or run a Sabbat game. Most players want some level of assurance their PCs will last long enough to get some solid roleplay. It is an extra challenge for an ST to do that while remaining true to the Sabbat. (And I understand why later Developers decided to turn the Sabbat into Camarilla-lite in order to avoid this problem. It just defeats the purpose of having the Sabbat as a setting element.)<br /> <br /> However, the game has always had a problem with this idea of assumed instant loyalty. There is a lot that gets passed over by many players and STs. For example, if you were embraced by the True Brujah in 2022, why would you care at all about the normal Brujah? You're not going to feel loyalty to some ancient antedeluvian who was destroyed thousands of years ago. You can't even argue that it will be done out of fear as the ordinary Brujah neither believe in the True Brujah or hunt them. Clan or bloodline loyalty should never be automatic especially the older the mortal who is embraced, and the more confidant he is thinking on his own. Clan culture and organization is only going to work over the long term. Loyalty earned in the short term will always need to be explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T00:06:49-07:00","id":1482579,"title":"","content":"The revised Creation Rites is something else from the original version. Most of how the Sabbat works was entirely upended for playability, even though you can still see a lot of authors (and players) stuck with the pre-revised ideas, which in my opinion is a shame. <br /> <br /> I like the term shovelhead, but even in revised, the way it is used is not to create new progeny, it is to create unliving weapons. No longer is humanity stripped, but it is more of a devastating blow to the psyche to be killed, embraces and then having to crawl up through the earth you were buried in - and then being herded and goaded towards an unknown enemy. It is probably also a tool of propaganda, from the Camarilla, on how dangerous the Sabbat is and how little concern they have for the masquerade, and innocent life.<br /> <br /> Have I as a player or as a ST been doing shovelheads? In pre-revised days, sure. Even in a post-revised LARP, but that was a sidetrack single-night event and none of the shovelheads survived.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I can\u2019t think of it. ST Transylvania Chronicles with a group that were exclusively Tzimsice, and they always choose their progeny. Granted they were elders when joining the Sabbat. They even murdered the Paris Sabbat for being slow, but they avoided mass embraces even then because of its unreliability. This was about 100 sessions without mass embraces.<br /> <br /> I played as a Sabbat, and I was the only one in the group to create progeny, two of them as an impulse thing related to the Toreador Antitribu weakness, with a third candidate being kept as a ghoul and undergoing the process of shedding her humanity and being indoctrinated into a path already before her embrace. The game ended before that, but she had probably been a ghoul for 45 out of the maybe 50 sessions, and would have gotten a normal embrace and hastened creation rites.<br /> <br /> Ran a game set in alternate LA, where the Sabbat had actually won when they fought the Anarchs. One of the player characters was a survivor from that and the closest to a shovelhead. Not buried, just embraced and shoved to the forefront. Earned his creation rites by surviving and being part of the siege. In none of the ~50 sessions did any player nor NPC perform a mass burial, but no player created a childe either. To be fair, this was just internal politics with no Camarilla (or Anarchs) involvement, and the only \u201chostile\u201d presence was some Setites, but they were to weak to pose a direct threat, so the idea to suddenly produce fodder probably never struck anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12225-trassel","name":"Trassel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T02:13:17-07:00","id":1482582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482556#post1482556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He didn't meant it as <i>your character is a shovelhead</i>, it was more <i>your character <b>embraces</b> shovelheads</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah my bad,<br /> <br /> Back on subject then My current lasombra does but she's picky about who, she'll lean towards other women around her age over guys and tries to be supportive and tends to try and get consent in some context. In our city theirs a guy who specifically preps shovelheads and she's made it clear she'll help train any lasombra in obtenerbration basics if needed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:28:03-07:00","id":1482625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482448-how-often-do-players-create-shovelheads-in-your-games?p=1482573#post1482573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the game has always had a problem with this idea of assumed instant loyalty. There is a lot that gets passed over by many players and STs. For example, if you were embraced by the True Brujah in 2022, why would you care at all about the normal Brujah? You're not going to feel loyalty to some ancient antedeluvian who was destroyed thousands of years ago. You can't even argue that it will be done out of fear as the ordinary Brujah neither believe in the True Brujah or hunt them. Clan or bloodline loyalty should never be automatic especially the older the mortal who is embraced, and the more confidant he is thinking on his own. Clan culture and organization is only going to work over the long term. Loyalty earned in the short term will always need to be explained.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another pet peeve of mine, but this one I mostly got tired of discussing long ago. I find the clan culture of most clans too tight to how the game describes Embraces and vampire life. The mere fact that vampires are too disperse and most live on their own means that the hold clan ideals have just by cultural influence should be minor.<br /> <br /> Some clans make sense because they have either a more gregarious environment and pressure to follow suit to a degree, or they start indoctrination before the actual Embrace.Nosferatu? Suit yourself if you want to strike on your own, you'll probably come back because the clan structure is for mutual survival. Giovanni? You're literally born in the Family and groomed for the Embrace. Tremere you may be a groomed candidate and indoctrinated as in a cult before the Embrace, but those who don't should be loyal mostly because they're not granted much choice, not because they feel like being &quot;of the blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> Most clans it only gets worse, and individual Kindred should derive their outlook more from the people they were before than from the clan's culture. There should be influence and interplay, not hard stereotypes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:37:35-07:00","id":1482674,"title":"","content":"I haven't played or storytold Sabbat yet for my Players. But I think it works just the same as the classical &quot;Mistake (maybe not) Out of Nowhere Embrace&quot; that so many Vampire videogames do. And I don't even believe that shovelheads most of the time get indoctrinated. Like... what better way to fuck a city's Prince than leaving a dozen of famished, lost, mad, ignorant and guideless vampires in his little Camarilla town? It's like setting bombs, only that its Masquerade breaching as hell, and will make the entire city and the Cam society have to move a lot of pieces and pull favors to take care of. And then they will be forced to lay down, while the Masquerade mends.. <br /> <br /> To raise a more organized shovelhead party I think it would take a week. And it would be more in the basis of threats and promises than anything, otherwise why the hell would these new pups give two shits about the war of sects? Best to throw them haphazardly against the enemy, full of hunger and despair. But, of course, you can do a pseudo-shovelhead Embrace where you actually train and indoctrinate them during a month or more, so they really turn into soldiers, but even then it would require more selection of the victims, and the strenght of them would still be the vinculum between them I think. <br /> <br /> Either way, I believe this tactic isn't so common, or at least works a bit differently. But it is a fun story hook, even to start a coterie or band without needing a lot of &quot;wow, a bunch of ignorant and sireless fledlings ended up together, what a coincidence&quot; or the need for a sect to preemptively select them together as Kindred. So I would definitely make a starting point for a Sabbat chronicle, be the PCs in this sect or not from that moment forward (in case they end up dealing with a very reasonable and calm Anarch, Autarkis or Camarilla).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:47:19-07:00","id":1482675,"title":"","content":"of the six players in my group, four are thinbloods that started their unlife as shovelheads (with the other two being a caitiff and a thinblood that they embraced) and they've encountered a few others as adversaries but that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T08:25:21-07:00","id":1482766,"title":"","content":"The only \u201cSabbat\u201d in my present game are technically ex-Sabbat; a pack that was mostly Honorable Accord in charge of a safe house for the wandering packs that, due to circumstances, never got the order to deploy on the Crusade and so, by the time it was figured out a few years later was entirely a case of \u201cI didn\u2019t leave the party, the party left me\u201d (the Sabbat having declared Honorable Accord no longer acceptable and all) and became effectively Anarchs by default (though they refer to themselves as being true Sabbat and that the things coming back from the Crusade are savages wearing Sabbat skins).<br /> <br /> They had done shovelheading in the past, but absent orders from above they recognize as legitimate they believe that it\u2019s use as a tool for growing what they see as the true Sabbat has past and, for the foreseeable future careful consideration of those who would grow their numbers is needed\u2026 if left unhindered they\u2019ll probably end up as a mini-sect of Vampire Knights (since the only Paths they\u2019re on are Honorable Accord and a Feral Heart) and their recruiting pitch will lean towards \u201cwe need you to join our elite order whose mission is to fight the Antediluvians and their agents (sold as \u201cthe greatest threat to ever exist.\u201d).\u201d If the campaign goes that long those NPCs will probably take to calling themselves The Knights of Caine or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T18:27:49-07:00","id":1482878,"title":"","content":"There is also one ex-Sabbat in my group, but he's just doing fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-04T09:01:35-07:00","id":1483039,"title":"","content":"I personally never used them at all. As we are playing mainly a Camarilla vs Anarch setting with the Sabbat largely gone with a few minor die hard packs that exist on the fringes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T07:35:26-07:00","id":1483125,"title":"","content":"My view of the shovelhead method is that it being unreliable is a Feature, not a bug. At least from a storytelling standpoint.<br /> <br /> No matter how effective it can be, it's still a reckless tactic. The Sabbat employs it in war because it's 1) cheap to do in terms of time and resources, and 2) prone to creating problems for their enemies even when it doesn't work out perfectly. From the perspective of the Sabbat, who have no care for human lives and have a &quot;it's the Camarilla's problem&quot; approach to the Masquerade (at least in Cam cities), there's little reason NOT to do it.<br /> <br /> Shovelheads are disposable. They don't need to be long-term recruits. They just need to be compelled using whatever bits of manipulation - promises, threats, isolation, cruelty, lies, or brute force - needed to get them from their graves to where they're being unleashed.<br /> <br /> If some of the shovelheads survive their suicidal charge, it's an unexpected bonus. If they just adamantly refuse to cooperate or try to escape, the Sabbat can either reclaim their blood, or just let them leave. It's not like a random mass embrace knows any tactical information about the Sabbat they could reveal. And if they cause Masquerade issues, again, that's the Camarilla's problem. It's why the tactic is done on crusade.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think the disconnect between early Sabbat and 2ndRevised Sabbat is really a deal-breaker. Roving bands of complete maniacs, mass embracing people for the evulz is not, in fact, incompatible with Sabbat who act like the Camarilla. It's a varied and politically complex sect, held together by blood magic and shared inhumanity. They codify these differences into factions, in fact. Loyalists do the &quot;roving bands&quot; thing from early VtM, while groups like the Ultra-Conservatives do the &quot;rigid, Camarilla-like hierarchy&quot;. That the Sabbat harbors Clans who maintain their pre-modern structures doesn't negate the existence of Cainites who reject all power structures.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think the disconnect between these ideals is part of the appeal of Revised+ Sabbat. There's a bunch of different vampires who each have their own wildly divergent opinions and unlifestyles. Which means there's not only a wide menu of options for Storytellers to choose from, but internal conflicts the ST can exploit for drama.<br /> <br /> There probably are packs for whom the mass embrace is their primary method of recruitment. If only because what started as just a war tactic became the default for them. If the pack is made up exclusively of second or third gen shovelheads, because their forebears all died, they might know no other way of doing things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}